WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:02.950
And our zip code of the day today,

2
00:00:02.950 --> 00:00:07.286
8-0-2-0-3, shout out to Denver, Colorado.

3
00:00:07.286 --> 00:00:08.119
(audience cheering)

4
00:00:08.119 --> 00:00:09.630
That's right!

5
00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:11.630
Hello, Denver!

6
00:00:11.630 --> 00:00:15.050
Home of our affiliate station, KCNC

7
00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:16.600
CBS 4.

8
00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:19.370
Now, Denver is nicknamed the Mile High City

9
00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:23.060
because it sits exactly one mile above sea level.

10
00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:27.070
The Denver Mint produces about 40 million coins a day

11
00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:30.140
and about 70% of that

12
00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:31.820
are pennies.

13
00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:34.570
I love pennies, especially picking up lucky pennies

14
00:00:34.570 --> 00:00:36.510
heads up on the street.

15
00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:39.670
It holds the second largest gold bullion deposit

16
00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:42.310
in the US, holding $100 billion

17
00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:46.300
worth of solid gold bars.

18
00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:49.420
Denver, Colorado, we would love to hear from you.

19
00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:51.120
Please send us some mail.

20
00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:52.950
Okay, now let's get started.

21
00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:54.230
We're gonna read our first letter.

22
00:00:54.230 --> 00:00:58.330
Just so you know, I open these for the first time on air.

23
00:00:58.330 --> 00:01:00.100
Makes it more fun.

24
00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:01.070
Okay.

25
00:01:01.070 --> 00:01:02.130
Let's see.

26
00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:03.444
Dear Drew and crew.

27
00:01:03.444 --> 00:01:07.200
(audience applauding)
(audience cheering)

28
00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:10.111
Hello Ashley from The Drewseum here.

29
00:01:10.111 --> 00:01:11.310
Oh!

30
00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:14.480
The Drewseum is this wonderful museum about me

31
00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:16.660
which is weird because I don't know why anyone

32
00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:17.493
would wanna do that,

33
00:01:17.493 --> 00:01:21.770
but here I have been enjoying the show so very much.

34
00:01:21.770 --> 00:01:23.820
My daughter and I were lucky enough

35
00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:25.920
to be VFFs a few weeks ago.

36
00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:28.290
She was inspired and wanted to send Drew some artwork.

37
00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:30.820
She asked me what's Drew's favorite thing besides children

38
00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:33.160
and I promptly answered mac and cheese.

39
00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:34.900
Ashley, you know me so well.

40
00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:37.210
So that was the motivation behind her cute drawing

41
00:01:37.210 --> 00:01:39.920
that we've enclosed and we hope you enjoy it.

42
00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:41.670
First of all, Ashley, don't be a stranger,

43
00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:43.193
we've hung out many times.

44
00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:47.110
Okay.

45
00:01:47.110 --> 00:01:50.800
Mila, thank you so much and I will be framing this

46
00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:52.970
and it will be going on my wall.

47
00:01:52.970 --> 00:01:55.060
In fact, let's see here.

48
00:01:55.060 --> 00:01:56.320
Why don't we just put it up right now,

49
00:01:56.320 --> 00:01:57.810
even though I hate putting a hole in it

50
00:01:57.810 --> 00:02:00.120
but I can fix that later.

51
00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:02.112
Okay, oh, God, hold on.

52
00:02:02.112 --> 00:02:03.059
(Drew sighing)

53
00:02:03.059 --> 00:02:05.900
(audience cheering)
(audience applauding)

54
00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:06.883
Look, Mila!

55
00:02:08.257 --> 00:02:09.390
I love it!

56
00:02:09.390 --> 00:02:11.630
Thank you, Mila and Ashley.

57
00:02:11.630 --> 00:02:12.860
Thanks, guys.

58
00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:16.170
Okay, our second letter is...

59
00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:18.110
Here we go.

60
00:02:18.110 --> 00:02:20.540
I'm old, 64.

61
00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:21.980
That's not old.

62
00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:24.810
For one of my first retirement adventures,

63
00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:27.730
I'd like to find and explore some mining properties

64
00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:30.640
that Howard Hughes owned and frequented.

65
00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:33.230
I purchased a retirement motorcycle.

66
00:02:33.230 --> 00:02:36.250
Cool, and a Jeep for these adventures

67
00:02:36.250 --> 00:02:38.850
but could use a new state-of-the-art metal detector

68
00:02:38.850 --> 00:02:41.690
to find Howard's artifacts, could you help?

69
00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:43.760
I'll split 'em with you.

70
00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:47.450
First of all, of course, Lance Campbell

71
00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:49.510
from Jackson, California.

72
00:02:49.510 --> 00:02:53.372
I am inspired by your plan, so I'm sending you $1,000.

73
00:02:53.372 --> 00:02:54.205
(audience cheering)
(audience applauding)

74
00:02:54.205 --> 00:02:56.830
So you can get that metal detector of your dreams

75
00:02:56.830 --> 00:02:58.490
and start your own adventure.

76
00:02:58.490 --> 00:03:01.333
I'm so happy for this chapter of your life.

77
00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:04.750
By the way, there is one request,

78
00:03:04.750 --> 00:03:06.660
will you send us some pictures and updates

79
00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:07.780
and keep in touch?

80
00:03:07.780 --> 00:03:08.913
Okay, thank you.

81
00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:14.090
We have time for one more, and this is from Trish Ramel

82
00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:16.713
in Sheboygan, Wisconsin.

83
00:03:17.710 --> 00:03:19.380
Dear Drew, I actually have a recipe box

84
00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:21.076
with actual recipe cards.

85
00:03:21.076 --> 00:03:21.909
(Drew gasping)

86
00:03:21.909 --> 00:03:24.020
I love them and I've shared them with many people

87
00:03:24.020 --> 00:03:28.330
and I ran out of people to give recipes to so, tag,

88
00:03:28.330 --> 00:03:30.020
I like your style, anyway,

89
00:03:30.020 --> 00:03:32.840
I can't believe you never ate spam,

90
00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:36.950
sent you a favorite recipe for mac salad with spam.

91
00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:38.900
Maybe you can test it on the show.

92
00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:41.930
I hope you like it, love, Trish.

93
00:03:41.930 --> 00:03:45.500
Okay, these recipes are absolutely

94
00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:46.850
gorgeous.

95
00:03:46.850 --> 00:03:49.660
I absolutely will cherish these.

96
00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:51.550
Thank you so much.

97
00:03:51.550 --> 00:03:52.910
This is treasure.

98
00:03:52.910 --> 00:03:54.250
Thank you.

99
00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:56.768
I'm really glad that you spammed me.

100
00:03:56.768 --> 00:03:57.620
(audience laughing)

101
00:03:57.620 --> 00:03:58.620
Get it?

102
00:03:58.620 --> 00:04:02.060
There's spam in my mailbox, but I'm not upset

103
00:04:02.060 --> 00:04:04.580
because you included these wonderful recipes

104
00:04:04.580 --> 00:04:06.950
and this absolute treasure, I love them.

105
00:04:06.950 --> 00:04:09.143
I have been wanting to try spam again.

106
00:04:10.940 --> 00:04:12.560
What's this?

107
00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:13.559
Thank you, Paulie.

108
00:04:13.559 --> 00:04:14.392
(audience laughing)

109
00:04:14.392 --> 00:04:15.225
Wait, what?

110
00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:19.720
Oh, my gosh.

111
00:04:19.720 --> 00:04:20.950
I'm like,

112
00:04:20.950 --> 00:04:22.490
macaroni

113
00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:23.620
salad?

114
00:04:23.620 --> 00:04:26.083
You sent the recipe, so we made it.

115
00:04:30.715 --> 00:04:32.090 line:15%
Trish!

116
00:04:32.090 --> 00:04:34.100 line:15%
Oh no, you didn't.

117
00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:35.870 line:15%
It's so good!

118
00:04:35.870 --> 00:04:39.720 line:15%
Recipe, mac salad, here it is, okay, Trish.

119
00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:43.780
One pound rotini, frozen peas, Miracle Whip,

120
00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:45.170
that's the taste.

121
00:04:45.170 --> 00:04:46.080
I love it.

122
00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:49.300
Yellow mustard, apple cider vinegar, sugar.

123
00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:51.830
Thank you so much!

124
00:04:51.830 --> 00:04:52.860
Thank you, Trish.

125
00:04:52.860 --> 00:04:56.860
Okay, if any of you guys out there want advice, help,

126
00:04:56.860 --> 00:04:58.750
maybe you wanna try something new,

127
00:04:58.750 --> 00:05:01.350
mail me your questions, requests, photos,

128
00:05:01.350 --> 00:05:04.670
funny or heartfelt stories, and to find out more,

129
00:05:04.670 --> 00:05:08.053 line:15%
get our address, go to TheDrewBarrymoreShow.com/DearDrew.

130
00:05:09.510 --> 00:05:12.970 line:15%
I can't wait to read more of your letters live on the show.

131
00:05:12.970 --> 00:05:15.010
Ashley and Mila and Lance and Trish,

132
00:05:15.010 --> 00:05:16.910
thank you so much for your letters.

133
00:05:16.910 --> 00:05:19.773
And here are my postcards to you.

134
00:05:20.810 --> 00:05:21.703
That, okay.

135
00:05:26.010 --> 00:05:27.830
Truly yours, Drew.

136
00:05:27.830 --> 00:05:30.413 line:15%
(upbeat music)

